<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh inflation rises to 2.1 percent in January.</title>
<headline>Kazakh inflation rises to 2.1 percent in January.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kazakh consumer price inflation quickened to 2.1 percent in January from 0.8 percent in December, the State Statistics Committee said on Thursday.</p>
<p>    KAZAKH CONSUMER PRICES     Jan '97     Dec '96     Jan '96</p>
<p>    Month-on-month pct change     +2.1	  +0.8	  +4.1</p>
<p>    Year-on-year pct change	+26.2	 +28.7	 +53.3</p>
<p>The government is forecasting a fall in annual inflation this year to 21 percent from 28.7 percent in 1996.</p>
<p>-- Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
